From 86bc94a8bf4fadfddc319e0d7c6302885216285c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] SCUMM: Add an extended bitmap font format with 8bpp
 coverage

The fan translation .fnt holds 1bpp glyphs in a fixed 2350 entry grid and
says nothing about itself: no glyph count, no encoding, no baseline. It
cannot carry anti-aliasing, so smooth text needed FreeType at run time
even though the glyphs never change.

SVFN puts that in the file instead. A 32 byte header names the code page,
the glyph count, the cell box and the baseline; glyphs are 1bpp or 8bpp
coverage, optionally with a per-glyph advance. The 8bpp values go into
the same channel a rasterised TrueType glyph would fill, so the composite
step blends them exactly as before.

Files are told apart by a magic. Every one of the 34 fan translation
fonts checked starts with a 2 and matches the 1bpp size exactly, so the
old path stays untouched.

scripts/mkfont.py bakes one from a TrueType face. Rendering a Noto Sans
CJK at 24px gives identical output on a build with FreeType and one
configured with --disable-freetype2.
